Lares (Tasked Spirit / Sol). Line numbers refer to the composed train.

* ''HIGH — MEASURED, ralias:'' `packages/lararium-node/src/vessel-private.ts:131` trusts the face gate, whose catalog bridge at `packages/lararium-node/src/face-fleet-view.ts:127` admits aliases. With two bootstrap faces, the real composed share verdict denied face A access to face B’s protected circles document. Adding an ordinary catalog pointer to that document changed denial to admission. Enforce private-plane ownership by document ID before consulting the bridge.

* ''HIGH — MEASURED, rcx:'' `packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-kel.ts:592` checks three distinct keys at threshold two without excluding self-recovery. Directly enrolling `[self, contact A, contact B]`, then rotating with ''self + contact A'', passed both `mintPersonaRotation` and full-chain verification. The friendly enrolment helper’s exclusion does not protect the KEL reader. Enforce it at reveal, including subsequent grafts.

* ''CROSS-LANE — HIGH LEAD, porch5 × ralias:'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-dispatcher.ts:357` triggers wiki mounting from the typed denial; `packages/lararium-tw5/src/vessel-residency-wiring.ts:205` resolves the wiki document through a catalog pointer. Meanwhile, `packages/lararium-node/src/self-slot-share.ts:142` admits in-process islands outside the private-document wire guard. ''Lead runs:'' alias a cold wiki to another face’s private plane and trigger the real fenced mount path. Confirm that materialization exposes no foreign tiddlers. This remains a source-backed lead, without an end-to-end leak measurement.

The probes used patched source in memory, without dist, builds, sockets, or the battery. Porch5’s delegation abort and answer controls both cleared their entries. The renamed source references were consistent; the declared alpha format cut was intentional.

Writing `out.md` was rejected by the read-only sandbox and approval settings. The handback therefore remains here.

